{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>A son of old age.</b> Born to him at the time of his old age. And Onkelos rendered it בַּר חַכִּים הוּא לֵהּ — everything he learned from Shem and Ever he handed on to him. Another interpretation: the radiance of his countenance was like his." "<b>Of fine wool.</b> A term of a garment of wool, like כַּרְפַּס and תְּכֵלֶת, and like the כְּתֹנֶת הַפַּסִּים of Tamar and Amnon. And the midrashic interpretation — after his troubles, for he was sold to Potiphar and to the traders and to the Ishmaelites and to the Midianites."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 37, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:02:22.335873847Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}